:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) Copyright Quartz Systems 2026.
:HELP NAME=ENDJRN.End Journal (ENDJRN)
:P.Use the End Journal (ENDJRN) command to end journaling of IFS
objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/OBJFID'.File identifier (OBJFID)
:P.The file identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OBJ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/PATTERN'.Name pattern (PATTERN)
:P.The name pattern for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pattern
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ENDJRN/LOGLVL'.Logging level (LOGLVL)
:P.How much of the job's messages are written to the job log, from 0
(none) to 4 (all).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ERRORS.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=STRJRN.Start Journal (STRJRN)
:P.Use the Start Journal (STRJRN) command to start journaling IFS
objects.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/OBJ'.Objects (OBJ)
:P.The object or objects the command works on, by name and library.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Name
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/OBJFID'.File identifier (OBJFID)
:P.The file identifier for this command.
:P.Up to 300 values can be given.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/JRN'.Journal (JRN)
:P.The journal, by name and library.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 5000 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/SUBTREE'.Directory subtree (SUBTREE)
:P.Whether the objects in the subdirectories are included.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.The objects of the directory only.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.The directory and everything below it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/PATTERN'.Name pattern (PATTERN)
:P.The name pattern for this command.
:P.Up to 20 values can be given.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Pattern
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 255 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '*' is used.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Include or omit
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*INCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.Included.
:PT.:PK.*OMIT:EPK.
:PD.Left out.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/INHERIT'.New objects inherit journaling (INHERIT)
:P.Whether to new objects inherit journaling.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/IMAGES'.Images (IMAGES)
:P.The images for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AFTER:EPK.
:PD.After the reference entry.
:PT.:PK.*BOTH:EPK.
:PD.Both.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/OMTJRNE'.Omit journal entry (OMTJRNE)
:P.The omit journal entry for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPNCLO.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='STRJRN/LOGLVL'.Logging level (LOGLVL)
:P.How much of the job's messages are written to the job log, from 0
(none) to 4 (all).
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *ERRORS.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
